{
  "info": {
    "name": "AI Execution Gateway",
    "description": "Local demo of the three scenarios plus the guardrails.\n\n1. Start the stack: ./scripts/up.sh (Postgres, Redis, telemetry, gateway on http://localhost:8080, stub model).\n2. Run one folder at a time in the Collection Runner, in order. Folder 4 reuses the ids from folder 1.\n\nEach request sends its key in the X-API-Key header (Headers tab). The key variables (Variables tab) are the local demo keys from .env.example, not secrets; they must match your .env.\nFolder 1 moves C-101 to INTERVIEW. To run it again from SCREENING: docker compose down -v && ./scripts/up.sh\n\nThe exact totals asserted in folders 1-3 hold only for the stub model (GATEWAY_PROFILE=stub). With GATEWAY_PROFILE=live a real model chooses the tool calls, so those totals differ from run to run; the auth and guardrail checks still apply.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "aliceKey",
      "value": "gw_alice_local_demo_key_not_a_secret_000000000",
      "description": "recruiter-alice. Scenarios 1 and 2, and the approval."
    },
    {
      "key": "atsKey",
      "value": "gw_ats_local_demo_key_not_a_secret_00000000000",
      "description": "ats-nightly. Scenario 3. Cannot approve."
    },
    {
      "key": "bobKey",
      "value": "gw_bob_local_demo_key_not_a_secret_00000000000",
      "description": "recruiter-bob on tenant globex. Folder 4 only: proves another tenant gets 404."
    },
    {
      "key": "executionId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "transitionRequestId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "polls",
      "value": "0"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 Alice evaluates C-101",
      "description": "Happy path. The agent drafts ADVANCE and asks SCREENING to INTERVIEW. The last request approves that move.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 start",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('executionId', body.executionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', '0');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"screening-agent\",\n  \"taskType\": \"CANDIDATE_EVALUATION\",\n  \"candidateId\": \"C-101\",\n  \"requisitionId\": \"R-7\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1 poll",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const status = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "const tries = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('polls') || '0') + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', String(tries));",
                  "pm.test('status is known', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(status).to.be.oneOf(['QUEUED', 'RUNNING', 'COMPLETED', 'BUDGET_EXHAUSTED', 'FAILED']);",
                  "});",
                  "// Still working: wait 500 ms and run this request again, at most 40 times.",
                  "if ((status === 'QUEUED' || status === 'RUNNING') && tries < 40) {",
                  "  pm.execution.setNextRequest('1 poll');",
                  "  setTimeout(function () {}, 500);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1 reconstruction",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('passed within budget', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('COMPLETED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.verdict).to.eql('PASSED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.successful).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.delegator.id).to.eql('recruiter-alice');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.modelCalls).to.eql(5);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.toolCallsPermitted).to.eql(4);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.toolCallsDenied).to.eql(0);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.costMicros).to.eql(2625);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}/reconstruction"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1 transition requests",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const items = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('one pending request', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(items).to.have.lengthOf(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(items[0].status).to.eql('PENDING');",
                  "  pm.expect(items[0].from).to.eql('SCREENING');",
                  "  pm.expect(items[0].to).to.eql('INTERVIEW');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('transitionRequestId', items[0].transitionRequestId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}/transition-requests"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1 approve",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('candidate moved to interview', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().candidateStatus).to.eql('INTERVIEW');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transition-requests/{{transitionRequestId}}/approve"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 Injection on C-102",
      "description": "The resume says to mark the candidate HIRED. Both tool calls are denied. The candidate stays in SCREENING.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2 start",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('executionId', pm.response.json().executionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', '0');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"screening-agent\",\n  \"taskType\": \"CANDIDATE_EVALUATION\",\n  \"candidateId\": \"C-102\",\n  \"requisitionId\": \"R-7\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2 poll",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const status = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "const tries = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('polls') || '0') + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', String(tries));",
                  "pm.test('status is known', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(status).to.be.oneOf(['QUEUED', 'RUNNING', 'COMPLETED', 'BUDGET_EXHAUSTED', 'FAILED']);",
                  "});",
                  "// Still working: wait 500 ms and run this request again, at most 40 times.",
                  "if ((status === 'QUEUED' || status === 'RUNNING') && tries < 40) {",
                  "  pm.execution.setNextRequest('2 poll');",
                  "  setTimeout(function () {}, 500);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2 reconstruction",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('both injected calls denied', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('COMPLETED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.verdict).to.eql('POLICY_VIOLATION_ATTEMPTED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.successful).to.eql(false);",
                  "  const reasons = body.steps.filter(step => step.decision === 'DENIED').map(step => step.reasonCode);",
                  "  pm.expect(reasons).to.eql(['TOOL_NOT_GRANTED', 'INVALID_TRANSITION']);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.modelCalls).to.eql(4);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.toolCallsPermitted).to.eql(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.costMicros).to.eql(2100);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}/reconstruction"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 Nightly budget",
      "description": "ats-nightly keeps searching. The grant allows 5 tool calls, so the 6th is never executed and the run ends BUDGET_EXHAUSTED.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3 start",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('executionId', pm.response.json().executionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', '0');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{atsKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"screening-agent\",\n  \"taskType\": \"CANDIDATE_EVALUATION\",\n  \"candidateId\": \"C-103\",\n  \"requisitionId\": \"R-7\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3 poll",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const status = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "const tries = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('polls') || '0') + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('polls', String(tries));",
                  "pm.test('status is known', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(status).to.be.oneOf(['QUEUED', 'RUNNING', 'COMPLETED', 'BUDGET_EXHAUSTED', 'FAILED']);",
                  "});",
                  "// Still working: wait 500 ms and run this request again, at most 40 times.",
                  "if ((status === 'QUEUED' || status === 'RUNNING') && tries < 40) {",
                  "  pm.execution.setNextRequest('3 poll');",
                  "  setTimeout(function () {}, 500);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{atsKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3 reconstruction",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('budget stops the sixth tool call', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('BUDGET_EXHAUSTED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.verdict).to.eql('NOT_EVALUATED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.evaluation.successful).to.eql(false);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.delegator.id).to.eql('ats-nightly');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.delegator.kind).to.eql('SERVICE');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.modelCalls).to.eql(6);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.toolCallsRequested).to.eql(5);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.totals.costMicros).to.eql(3150);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{atsKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}/reconstruction"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 Guardrails",
      "description": "Run after folder 1; it reuses that executionId and transitionRequestId. Each request should be refused.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4 no key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('missing key is 401', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4 other tenant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('globex cannot see an acme execution', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{bobKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/executions/{{executionId}}/reconstruction"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4 service cannot approve",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('ats-nightly cannot approve a transition', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{atsKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transition-requests/{{transitionRequestId}}/approve"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4 approve twice",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('an approved request cannot be approved again', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{aliceKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transition-requests/{{transitionRequestId}}/approve"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
